Kubernetes vs AWS Load Balancer – Who’s the Real Traffic Handler?

"Type: LoadBalancer" likhne se kya Kubernetes khud load balancing karta hai?
Ya AWS ka ELB actual traffic manage karta hai?

Bhai, ye doubt har DevOps fresher ke dimaag me hota hi hai — aur honestly, ye sirf surface se samajh aata hai, depth me jao toh picture clear hoti hai.

Chal aaj ek baar me samjhte hain — easy language me, real clarity ke saath  

What really happens when you create a LoadBalancer service in Kubernetes?
Imagine you write this:
type: LoadBalancer

Looks fancy, right?
Lekin asli game uske baad shuru hoti hai 

Kubernetes khud se koi load balancer create nahi karta.
Kubernetes bolta hai cloud provider ko (AWS/GCP/Azure):
      “Bhai, ek external Load Balancer de do jo mera traffic handle kare.”
AWS ke paas Cloud Controller Manager ka request jaata hai
AWS ELB (Elastic Load Balancer) bana deta hai —
aur uske peeche worker nodes ke IPs register kar deta hai.


Par AWS ko kaise pata chalta ki kaunse node IPs register karne hai?
Ye bhi Kubernetes hi batata hai bhai!
Cloud Controller Manager:
       kubectl get nodes se sab nodes ki internal ya external IPs read karta hai
Phir AWS ko bolta hai:
       “Yeh mere active worker nodes hain — inko ELB ke backend me daal de”
Bas.
 
Ab AWS ELB ready hai traffic leke NodePort pe forward karne ke liye.


Traffic ka actual flow kaise hota hai?
User hits the ELB DNS (like https://lnkd.in/dwa4PEkz)

ELB forwards the request to any one of the Node IPs + NodePort

Wahan pe kube-proxy hota hai, jo traffic ko aage actual pod tak le jaata hai
Yeh routing Kubernetes handle karta hai — but first gate pe standing guard = AWS Load Balancer.


So, who’s the real traffic boss?
Not Kubernetes.
 It just acts as a middleman.
The actual traffic entry, balancing, health checks — sab kuch cloud load balancer handle karta hai.



Summary in simple words:
Kubernetes: “Mujhe ek Load Balancer chahiye”
Cloud Provider: “Lo bhai, ELB le lo”
Kubernetes: “In nodes ko backend me daal de”
AWS: “Done. Ab traffic mera kaam”

So next time jab koi puche — "K8s me LoadBalancer ka actual role kya hai?"
 Tere paas answer ready hai — confidently boliyo:
      “Kubernetes doesn’t do external load balancing. It requests and registers cloud load balancers — actual traffic handling is done by AWS ELB.”
